== Bugs ==
*The {{AN|Looting}} perk does not work on collection items that are dropped directly in compacted forms, such as {{Item|Silver Magmafish}}.

== Tips ==
*The Black Cat Pet is utilized in [[Dungeons]] by players seeking efficiency, as the pet gives a sizable increase in {{stat|spd}} and increases the {{stat|spd}} cap, which is highly useful in [[Dungeons]] as only one potion, including effects that increase the {{stat|spd}} stat, can be applied during each run, which significantly increases the difficulty of getting higher {{stat|spd}} inside [[Dungeons]].
*Due to increasing your speed cap by {{Green|100}} with any [[Armor/Sets|armor set]], this pet can be paired with the {{Item|Warden Helmet}} to boost its damage by +40% on top of its original bonus.
*The Black Cat Pet is often paired with Sorrow Armor for higher Magic Find, increasing the odds of rare drops.

==Trivia== 
*Upon release, the Black Cat Pet cost {{Item|Purple Candy|amount=2,500}}, which made it impossible to purchase since a player's inventory is unable to hold that many candies. Upon further release, the Black Cat Pet price was reduced to {{Item|Purple Candy|amount=2,000}}, making it purchasable.
* For a couple months after the [[Spooky Festival]]'s release, {{NPCSprite|George}} bought the Black Cat Pet for {{c|20000000}}, which was far more than its material cost, however this stayed in the game for multiple months because of the limited awareness of this exploit.
**{{NPCSprite|George}} now buys Black Cat Pets for {{c|5000000}}, which is roughly less than a fourth of its material cost.
*It looks almost identical to the {{Item|Cat Talisman}} with its eyes being more blue than the teal eyes of the {{Item|Cat Talisman}}.
*In game, the Black Cat Pet improves your luck, however, in some places in real life, black cats are associated with bad luck and misfortune.

